IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cla-nouns`
IMPORT `sgia-p1-definitions`

-- Civil Law Act 1909 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (version in force from 15/10/2024)
-- LAYER 1 -- sections 6 to 9: contracts that must be evidenced in writing, trusts of immovable property and
-- dispositions of equitable interests, the rule in Bain v Fothergill, continuity of contracts on the euro.
--
-- "Immovable property" is the Interpretation Act's term (s 2(1), a definition that "includes" land, benefits to arise out of
-- land and things attached to the earth).  s 6(d) reads it from the copied module sgia-p1-definitions.l4 (see NOTES.md,
-- "Dependencies").
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE are answers the Act gives in its own words; NOTHING is "the Act does not answer".

§ `Section 6 -- contracts which must be evidenced in writing`

-- src:805 | 6. No action shall be brought against —
-- src:807 | (a) any executor or administrator upon any special promise to
-- src:808 | answer damages out of his own estate;
-- src:810 | (b) any defendant upon any special promise to answer for the
-- src:811 | debt, default or miscarriage of another person;
-- src:813 | (c) any person upon any agreement made upon consideration
-- src:814 | of marriage;
-- src:816 | (d) any person upon any contract for the sale or other
-- src:817 | disposition of immovable property, or any interest in
-- src:818 | such property; or
-- src:820 | (e) any person upon any agreement that is not to be performed
-- src:821 | within the space of one year from the making thereof,
-- src:826 | unless the promise or agreement upon which such action is brought,
-- src:827 | or some memorandum or note thereof, is in writing and signed by the
-- src:828 | party to be charged therewith or some other person lawfully
-- src:829 | authorised by him.
@ref s 6 (src:805-829)
GIVEN `the kind of action` IS A `Kind of action under section 6`
      `the promise or agreement or some memorandum or note of it is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is signed by the party to be charged or by some other person lawfully authorised by that party` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 6 an action may be brought on the promise or agreement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the kind of action` EQUALS `Another kind of action` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the five heads (a) to (e) name the actions the bar reaches
        IF `the promise or agreement or some memorandum or note of it is in writing` AND `it is signed by the party to be charged or by some other person lawfully authorised by that party` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless the promise or agreement ... is in writing and signed" -- a lifted bar grants nothing (fork QA); see the companion s 6 the action is barred for want of a signed writing
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No action shall be brought against"

-- src:805 | 6. No action shall be brought against —
-- src:807 | (a) any executor or administrator upon any special promise to
-- src:808 | answer damages out of his own estate;
-- src:810 | (b) any defendant upon any special promise to answer for the
-- src:811 | debt, default or miscarriage of another person;
-- src:813 | (c) any person upon any agreement made upon consideration
-- src:814 | of marriage;
-- src:816 | (d) any person upon any contract for the sale or other
-- src:817 | disposition of immovable property, or any interest in
-- src:818 | such property; or
-- src:820 | (e) any person upon any agreement that is not to be performed
-- src:821 | within the space of one year from the making thereof,
-- src:826 | unless the promise or agreement upon which such action is brought,
-- src:827 | or some memorandum or note thereof, is in writing and signed by the
-- src:828 | party to be charged therewith or some other person lawfully
-- src:829 | authorised by him.
@ref s 6 the bar as a yes/no question (src:805-829)
GIVEN `the kind of action` IS A `Kind of action under section 6`
      `the promise or agreement or some memorandum or note of it is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is signed by the party to be charged or by some other person lawfully authorised by that party` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 6 the action is barred for want of a signed writing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the kind of action` EQUALS `Another kind of action` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the five heads (a) to (e) name the actions the bar reaches
        IF `the promise or agreement or some memorandum or note of it is in writing` AND `it is signed by the party to be charged or by some other person lawfully authorised by that party` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the promise or agreement upon which such action is brought, or some memorandum or note thereof, is in writing and signed by the party to be charged therewith or some other person lawfully authorised by him" -- the bar does not apply
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:816 | (d) any person upon any contract for the sale or other
-- src:817 | disposition of immovable property, or any interest in
-- src:818 | such property; or
@ref s 6(d) with the Interpretation Act s 2(1) "immovable property" (src:816-818)
GIVEN `the kind of property` IS A `Kind of property`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 6(d) the property is immovable property` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind of property`
    WHEN Land THEN JUST (elem "land" (`what the Act names in defining` "immovable property"))
    WHEN `A benefit to arise out of land` THEN JUST (elem "benefits to arise out of land" (`what the Act names in defining` "immovable property"))
    WHEN `A thing attached to the earth` THEN JUST (elem "things attached to the earth or permanently fastened to anything attached to the earth" (`what the Act names in defining` "immovable property"))
    WHEN `A thing permanently fastened to anything attached to the earth` THEN JUST (elem "things attached to the earth or permanently fastened to anything attached to the earth" (`what the Act names in defining` "immovable property"))
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“immovable property” includes land, benefits to arise out of land and things attached to the earth" (Interpretation Act s 2(1)): the list is not closed

§ `Section 7 -- trusts of immovable property and dispositions of equitable interests`

-- src:834 | 7.—(1) A declaration of trust respecting any immovable property
-- src:835 | or any interest in such property must be manifested and proved by
-- src:836 | some writing signed by some person who is able to declare such trust
-- src:837 | or by his will.
@ref s 7(1) (src:834-837)
GIVEN `the declaration of trust respects immovable property or an interest in it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is manifested and proved by some writing signed by some person who is able to declare the trust` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made by his will` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(1) the declaration of trust is manifested and proved as the subsection requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the declaration of trust respects immovable property or an interest in it` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A declaration of trust respecting any immovable property or any interest in such property"
        IF `it is manifested and proved by some writing signed by some person who is able to declare the trust` OR `it is made by his will` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "must" (fork QB); the subsection does not say what follows if the requirement is not met

-- src:839 | (2) A disposition of an equitable interest or trust subsisting at the
-- src:840 | time of the disposition must be in writing signed by the person
-- src:841 | disposing of the same or by his agent lawfully authorised in writing or
-- src:842 | by will.
@ref s 7(2) (src:839-842)
GIVEN `the disposition is of an equitable interest or trust subsisting at the time of the disposition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in writing signed by the person disposing of it or by his agent lawfully authorised in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made by will` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(2) the disposition of the equitable interest or trust is in writing as the subsection requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the disposition is of an equitable interest or trust subsisting at the time of the disposition` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A disposition of an equitable interest or trust subsisting at the time of the disposition"
        IF `it is in writing signed by the person disposing of it or by his agent lawfully authorised in writing` OR `it is made by will` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "must" (fork QB); the subsection does not say what follows if the requirement is not met

-- src:844 | (3) This section does not affect the creation or operation of
-- src:845 | resulting, implied or constructive trusts.
@ref s 7(3) (src:844-845)
GIVEN `the trust is a resulting implied or constructive trust` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(3) section 7 affects the creation or operation of the trust` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the trust is a resulting implied or constructive trust` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not affect the creation or operation of resulting, implied or constructive trusts"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "resulting, implied or constructive trusts"

§ `Section 8 -- the rule in Bain v Fothergill`

-- src:849 | 8. The rule of law known as the rule in Bain v Fothergill is
-- src:850 | abolished in relation to contracts made on or after 1 January 1999.
@ref s 8 (src:849-850)
GIVEN `the date on which the contract was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8 the rule in Bain v Fothergill is abolished in relation to the contract` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the date on which the contract was made` AT LEAST (Date 1 1 1999) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in relation to contracts made on or after 1 January 1999" -- a scope limit with no "only": the section is silent on an earlier contract (fork F-S8)

§ `Section 9 -- continuity of contracts on the euro`

-- src:855 | 9.—(1) It is declared for the avoidance of doubt that —
-- src:857 | (a) if a subject or medium of payment of a contract,
-- src:858 | agreement, deed, security or other instrument is a
-- src:859 | currency that has been substituted or replaced by the
-- src:860 | euro, the euro shall be a commercially reasonable
-- src:861 | substitute and substantial equivalent that may be —
-- src:863 | (i) used in determining the value of such currency; or
-- src:865 | (ii) tendered, in each case at the conversion rate
-- src:866 | specified in, and otherwise calculated in
-- src:867 | accordance with, the applicable regulations adopted
-- src:868 | by the Council of the EU;
@ref s 9(1)(a) (src:855-868)
GIVEN `the subject or medium of payment is a currency that has been substituted or replaced by the euro` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use of the euro` IS A `Use of the euro under section 9(1)`
      `the conversion rate is the rate specified in and calculated in accordance with the applicable regulations adopted by the Council of the EU` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(1)(a) the euro is a commercially reasonable substitute and substantial equivalent for the substituted currency` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the subject or medium of payment is a currency that has been substituted or replaced by the euro` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if a subject or medium of payment ... is a currency that has been substituted or replaced by the euro"
        IF `the use of the euro` EQUALS `Used in another way` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "that may be — (i) used in determining the value of such currency; or (ii) tendered"
        IF `the conversion rate is the rate specified in and calculated in accordance with the applicable regulations adopted by the Council of the EU` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in each case at the conversion rate specified in, and otherwise calculated in accordance with, the applicable regulations adopted by the Council of the EU"

-- src:873 | (b) if a subject or medium of payment of a contract,
-- src:874 | agreement, deed, security or instrument is the Ecu, the
-- src:875 | euro shall be a commercially reasonable substitute and
-- src:876 | substantial equivalent that may be —
-- src:878 | (i) used in determining the value of the Ecu; or
-- src:880 | (ii) tendered, in each case at the conversion rate
-- src:881 | specified in, and otherwise calculated in
-- src:882 | accordance with, the applicable regulations adopted
-- src:883 | by the Council of the EU.
@ref s 9(1)(b) (src:873-883)
GIVEN `the subject or medium of payment is the Ecu` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use of the euro` IS A `Use of the euro under section 9(1)`
      `the conversion rate is the rate specified in and calculated in accordance with the applicable regulations adopted by the Council of the EU` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(1)(b) the euro is a commercially reasonable substitute and substantial equivalent for the Ecu` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the subject or medium of payment is the Ecu` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if a subject or medium of payment of a contract, agreement, deed, security or instrument is the Ecu"
        IF `the use of the euro` EQUALS `Used in another way` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "that may be — (i) used in determining the value of the Ecu; or (ii) tendered"
        IF `the conversion rate is the rate specified in and calculated in accordance with the applicable regulations adopted by the Council of the EU` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in each case at the conversion rate specified in, and otherwise calculated in accordance with, the applicable regulations adopted by the Council of the EU"

-- src:885 | (2) It is declared for the avoidance of doubt that to the extent the
-- src:886 | performance of any of the obligations set out in subsection (1) may,
-- src:887 | apart from the introduction of the euro, be made in the currency or
-- src:888 | currencies originally designated in such contract, agreement, deed,
-- src:889 | security or other instrument, such performance may be made in such
-- src:890 | currency or currencies (so long as such currency or currencies remain
-- src:891 | legal tender) or in euro, but not in any other currency, whether or not
-- src:892 | such other currency —
-- src:894 | (a) has been substituted or replaced by the euro; or
-- src:896 | (b) is a currency that is considered a denomination of the euro
-- src:897 | and has a fixed conversion rate with respect to the euro.
@ref s 9(2) (src:885-897)
GIVEN `the performance could apart from the introduction of the euro be made in the currency or currencies originally designated in the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the currency of performance` IS A `Currency of performance`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(2) performance may be made in the currency` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the performance could apart from the introduction of the euro be made in the currency or currencies originally designated in the instrument` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to the extent the performance of any of the obligations set out in subsection (1) may, apart from the introduction of the euro, be made in the currency or currencies originally designated"
        IF `the currency of performance` EQUALS `The currency originally designated in the instrument and still legal tender` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the currency of performance` EQUALS `The euro` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the currency of performance` EQUALS `The currency originally designated in the instrument but no longer legal tender` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(so long as such currency or currencies remain legal tender)"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but not in any other currency, whether or not such other currency — (a) has been substituted or replaced by the euro; or (b) is a currency that is considered a denomination of the euro"

-- src:899 | (3) It is declared for the avoidance of doubt that none of the
-- src:900 | following events shall have the effect of discharging or excusing
-- src:901 | performance under any contract, agreement, deed, security or
-- src:902 | instrument, or give a party the right to unilaterally alter or
-- src:903 | terminate any contract, agreement, deed, security or instrument:
-- src:905 | (a) the introduction of the euro;
-- src:907 | (b) the tendering of euros in connection with any obligation in
-- src:908 | compliance with paragraph (a) or (b) of subsection (1);
-- src:910 | (c) the determining of the value of any obligation in
-- src:911 | compliance with paragraph (a) or (b) of subsection (1);
-- src:913 | (d) the calculating or determining of the subject or medium of
-- src:914 | payment of a contract, agreement, deed, security or
-- src:915 | instrument with reference to interest rate or other basis
-- src:916 | that has been substituted or replaced due to the introduction
-- src:921 | of the euro and that is a reasonable substitute and
-- src:922 | substantial equivalent.
@ref s 9(3) (src:899-922)
GIVEN `the event` IS A `Event under section 9(3)`
      `the basis is a reasonable substitute and substantial equivalent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(3) the event discharges or excuses performance or gives a party the right to unilaterally alter or terminate the instrument` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the event` EQUALS `Another event` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraphs (a) to (d) name the events; the subsection does not say that no other event can discharge or excuse performance
        IF `the event` EQUALS `Calculating or determining the subject or medium of payment with reference to a basis substituted or replaced due to the introduction of the euro` AND (NOT `the basis is a reasonable substitute and substantial equivalent`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "that is a reasonable substitute and substantial equivalent"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "none of the following events shall have the effect of discharging or excusing performance under any contract, agreement, deed, security or instrument, or give a party the right to unilaterally alter or terminate"

-- src:924 | (4) The provisions of this section shall be subject to any agreement
-- src:925 | between parties with specific reference to or agreement regarding the
-- src:926 | introduction of the euro.
@ref s 9(4) (src:924-926)
GIVEN `the parties have an agreement with specific reference to or regarding the introduction of the euro` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(4) the provisions of section 9 give way to the agreement of the parties` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the parties have an agreement with specific reference to or regarding the introduction of the euro` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "subject to any agreement between parties with specific reference to or agreement regarding the introduction of the euro"; with no such agreement the subsection says nothing

-- src:928 | (5) Nothing in this section shall be construed so as to affect the
-- src:929 | validity or enforceability of any contract, agreement, deed, security or
-- src:930 | other instrument denominated in whole or in part in a currency
-- src:931 | affected by alteration in circumstances other than the introduction of
-- src:932 | the euro.
@ref s 9(5) (src:928-932)
GIVEN `the instrument is denominated in whole or in part in a currency affected by an alteration in circumstances other than the introduction of the euro` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(5) section 9 affects the validity or enforceability of the instrument` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the instrument is denominated in whole or in part in a currency affected by an alteration in circumstances other than the introduction of the euro` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section shall be construed so as to affect the validity or enforceability of any contract, agreement, deed, security or other instrument denominated in whole or in part in a currency affected by alteration in circumstances other than the introduction of the euro"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "denominated in whole or in part in a currency affected by alteration in circumstances other than the introduction of the euro" -- fork QE: "other than" limits what a flat negative covers, so the introduction of the euro itself gets NOTHING

-- src:934 | (6) For the purposes of this section —
-- src:936 | (a) “euro” means the currency of participating member states
-- src:937 | of the EU that adopt a single currency in accordance with
-- src:938 | the treaty on EU signed on 7 February 1992;
@ref s 9(6)(a) (src:934-938)
GIVEN `the currency is the currency of the participating member states of the EU that adopt a single currency in accordance with the treaty on EU signed on 7 February 1992` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(6)(a) the currency is the euro` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the currency is the currency of the participating member states of the EU that adopt a single currency in accordance with the treaty on EU signed on 7 February 1992` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“euro” means the currency of participating member states of the EU that adopt a single currency in accordance with the treaty on EU signed on 7 February 1992"

-- src:940 | (b) “introduction of the euro” means the implementation from
-- src:941 | time to time of economic and monetary union in member
-- src:942 | states of the EU in accordance with the treaty on EU signed
-- src:943 | on 7 February 1992;
@ref s 9(6)(b) (src:940-943)
GIVEN `the event is the implementation from time to time of economic and monetary union in member states of the EU in accordance with the treaty on EU signed on 7 February 1992` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(6)(b) the event is the introduction of the euro` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the event is the implementation from time to time of economic and monetary union in member states of the EU in accordance with the treaty on EU signed on 7 February 1992` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“introduction of the euro” means the implementation from time to time of economic and monetary union in member states of the EU"

-- src:945 | (c) “EU” means the European Union;
@ref s 9(6)(c) (src:945)
GIVEN `the body is the European Union` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(6)(c) the body is the EU` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the body is the European Union` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“EU” means the European Union"

-- src:947 | (d) “Ecu” or “European Currency Unit” means the currency
-- src:948 | basket that is from time to time used as the unit of account
-- src:949 | of the European Community as defined in European
-- src:950 | Council Regulation No. 3320/94;
@ref s 9(6)(d) (src:947-950)
GIVEN `the unit is the currency basket that is from time to time used as the unit of account of the European Community as defined in European Council Regulation No. 3320/94` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(6)(d) the unit is the Ecu` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the unit is the currency basket that is from time to time used as the unit of account of the European Community as defined in European Council Regulation No. 3320/94` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Ecu” or “European Currency Unit” means the currency basket that is from time to time used as the unit of account of the European Community"

-- src:952 | (e) when the euro first becomes the monetary unit of
-- src:953 | participating member states of the EU, references to the
-- src:954 | Ecu in a contract, agreement, deed, security or other
-- src:955 | instrument that also refers to such definition of the Ecu
-- src:956 | shall be replaced by references to the euro at a rate of one
-- src:957 | euro to one Ecu; and
@ref s 9(6)(e) (src:952-957)
GIVEN `the instrument also refers to such definition of the Ecu` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the euro has first become the monetary unit of the participating member states of the EU` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(6)(e) the reference to the Ecu is replaced by a reference to the euro at a rate of one euro to one Ecu` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the instrument also refers to such definition of the Ecu` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "references to the Ecu in a contract, agreement, deed, security or other instrument that also refers to such definition of the Ecu"
        IF `the euro has first become the monetary unit of the participating member states of the EU` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when the euro first becomes the monetary unit of participating member states of the EU" -- a "when" is read as "where" (ruling of 2026-11-05) -- MARGINAL (a): a failed "where" or "when" is the text's no (ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (b))

-- src:959 | (f) references to the Ecu in a contract, agreement, deed,
-- src:960 | security or other instrument without such a definition of the
-- src:961 | Ecu shall be presumed, unless it is shown that the parties
-- src:962 | intended otherwise, to be references to the currency basket
-- src:967 | that is from time to time used as the unit of account of the
-- src:968 | European Community.
@ref s 9(6)(f) (src:959-968)
GIVEN `the instrument refers to the Ecu without such a definition of the Ecu` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is shown that the parties intended otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(6)(f) the reference to the Ecu is presumed to be a reference to the currency basket` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the instrument refers to the Ecu without such a definition of the Ecu` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "references to the Ecu in a contract, agreement, deed, security or other instrument without such a definition of the Ecu"
        IF `it is shown that the parties intended otherwise` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless it is shown that the parties intended otherwise" -- a presumption lifted by an exception: the requirement does not apply
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `Sections 6 to 9 -- tests`

-- s 6: the five heads, with and without a signed writing
#ASSERT `s 6 an action may be brought on the promise or agreement` `Action on a special promise by an executor or administrator to answer damages out of his own estate` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- (a): "No action shall be brought against any executor or administrator"
#ASSERT `s 6 an action may be brought on the promise or agreement` `Action on a special promise to answer for the debt default or miscarriage of another person` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- (b)
#ASSERT `s 6 an action may be brought on the promise or agreement` `Action on an agreement made upon consideration of marriage` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- (c)
#ASSERT `s 6 an action may be brought on the promise or agreement` `Action on a contract for the sale or other disposition of immovable property or an interest in it` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- (d)
#ASSERT `s 6 an action may be brought on the promise or agreement` `Action on an agreement not to be performed within one year of its making` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- (e)
#ASSERT `s 6 an action may be brought on the promise or agreement` `Action on an agreement not to be performed within one year of its making` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- in writing but not signed
#ASSERT `s 6 an action may be brought on the promise or agreement` `Action on an agreement not to be performed within one year of its making` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- signed but no writing (the signature is of a writing)
#ASSERT `s 6 an action may be brought on the promise or agreement` `Action on an agreement not to be performed within one year of its making` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- "unless" met: a lifted bar grants nothing
#ASSERT `s 6 an action may be brought on the promise or agreement` `Another kind of action` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not one of the five heads
#ASSERT `s 6 the action is barred for want of a signed writing` `Action on an agreement made upon consideration of marriage` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- barred
#ASSERT `s 6 the action is barred for want of a signed writing` `Action on an agreement made upon consideration of marriage` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "unless ... in writing and signed": the bar does not apply
#ASSERT `s 6 the action is barred for want of a signed writing` `Action on an agreement made upon consideration of marriage` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- not signed
#ASSERT `s 6 the action is barred for want of a signed writing` `Another kind of action` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- outside the five heads
-- s 6(d) with the Interpretation Act definition
#ASSERT `s 6(d) the property is immovable property` Land EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "includes land"
#ASSERT `s 6(d) the property is immovable property` `A benefit to arise out of land` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "benefits to arise out of land"
#ASSERT `s 6(d) the property is immovable property` `A thing attached to the earth` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "things attached to the earth"
#ASSERT `s 6(d) the property is immovable property` `A thing permanently fastened to anything attached to the earth` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "permanently fastened to anything attached to the earth"
#ASSERT `s 6(d) the property is immovable property` `Some other kind of property` EQUALS NOTHING -- "includes" does not close the list
-- s 7
#ASSERT `s 7(1) the declaration of trust is manifested and proved as the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- signed writing
#ASSERT `s 7(1) the declaration of trust is manifested and proved as the subsection requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "or by his will"
#ASSERT `s 7(1) the declaration of trust is manifested and proved as the subsection requires` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- neither: a bare "must" (QB)
#ASSERT `s 7(1) the declaration of trust is manifested and proved as the subsection requires` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not a trust of immovable property
#ASSERT `s 7(2) the disposition of the equitable interest or trust is in writing as the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- in writing signed by the person disposing or his authorised agent
#ASSERT `s 7(2) the disposition of the equitable interest or trust is in writing as the subsection requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "or by will"
#ASSERT `s 7(2) the disposition of the equitable interest or trust is in writing as the subsection requires` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- an oral disposition: a bare "must" (QB)
#ASSERT `s 7(2) the disposition of the equitable interest or trust is in writing as the subsection requires` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not a disposition of an equitable interest or trust
#ASSERT `s 7(3) section 7 affects the creation or operation of the trust` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "does not affect the creation or operation of resulting, implied or constructive trusts"
#ASSERT `s 7(3) section 7 affects the creation or operation of the trust` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- an express trust: see (1)
-- s 8: the day it starts is 1 January 1999
#ASSERT `s 8 the rule in Bain v Fothergill is abolished in relation to the contract` (Date 1 1 1999) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "made on or after 1 January 1999"
#ASSERT `s 8 the rule in Bain v Fothergill is abolished in relation to the contract` (Date 31 12 1998) EQUALS NOTHING -- the day before: the section is silent
#ASSERT `s 8 the rule in Bain v Fothergill is abolished in relation to the contract` (Date 2 5 2024) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- later
-- s 9(1)
#ASSERT `s 9(1)(a) the euro is a commercially reasonable substitute and substantial equivalent for the substituted currency` TRUE `Used in determining the value of the currency or of the Ecu` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (a)(i)
#ASSERT `s 9(1)(a) the euro is a commercially reasonable substitute and substantial equivalent for the substituted currency` TRUE Tendered TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (a)(ii)
#ASSERT `s 9(1)(a) the euro is a commercially reasonable substitute and substantial equivalent for the substituted currency` TRUE Tendered FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not at the conversion rate in the regulations
#ASSERT `s 9(1)(a) the euro is a commercially reasonable substitute and substantial equivalent for the substituted currency` FALSE Tendered TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not a substituted currency
#ASSERT `s 9(1)(a) the euro is a commercially reasonable substitute and substantial equivalent for the substituted currency` TRUE `Used in another way` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- a use other than valuing or tendering
#ASSERT `s 9(1)(b) the euro is a commercially reasonable substitute and substantial equivalent for the Ecu` TRUE Tendered TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (b)(ii)
#ASSERT `s 9(1)(b) the euro is a commercially reasonable substitute and substantial equivalent for the Ecu` FALSE Tendered TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not the Ecu
-- s 9(2)
#ASSERT `s 9(2) performance may be made in the currency` TRUE `The currency originally designated in the instrument and still legal tender` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the original currency, still legal tender
#ASSERT `s 9(2) performance may be made in the currency` TRUE `The euro` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "or in euro"
#ASSERT `s 9(2) performance may be made in the currency` TRUE `The currency originally designated in the instrument but no longer legal tender` EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "so long as such currency or currencies remain legal tender"
#ASSERT `s 9(2) performance may be made in the currency` TRUE `Any other currency` EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "but not in any other currency"
#ASSERT `s 9(2) performance may be made in the currency` FALSE `Any other currency` EQUALS NOTHING -- performance could not in any case be in the original currency
-- s 9(3)
#ASSERT `s 9(3) the event discharges or excuses performance or gives a party the right to unilaterally alter or terminate the instrument` `The introduction of the euro` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- (a)
#ASSERT `s 9(3) the event discharges or excuses performance or gives a party the right to unilaterally alter or terminate the instrument` `The tendering of euros in compliance with section 9(1)(a) or (b)` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- (b)
#ASSERT `s 9(3) the event discharges or excuses performance or gives a party the right to unilaterally alter or terminate the instrument` `The determining of the value of an obligation in compliance with section 9(1)(a) or (b)` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- (c)
#ASSERT `s 9(3) the event discharges or excuses performance or gives a party the right to unilaterally alter or terminate the instrument` `Calculating or determining the subject or medium of payment with reference to a basis substituted or replaced due to the introduction of the euro` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- (d), a reasonable substitute
#ASSERT `s 9(3) the event discharges or excuses performance or gives a party the right to unilaterally alter or terminate the instrument` `Calculating or determining the subject or medium of payment with reference to a basis substituted or replaced due to the introduction of the euro` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- (d), not a reasonable substitute
#ASSERT `s 9(3) the event discharges or excuses performance or gives a party the right to unilaterally alter or terminate the instrument` `Another event` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not listed
-- s 9(4) to (6)
#ASSERT `s 9(4) the provisions of section 9 give way to the agreement of the parties` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "subject to any agreement"
#ASSERT `s 9(4) the provisions of section 9 give way to the agreement of the parties` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- no such agreement
#ASSERT `s 9(5) section 9 affects the validity or enforceability of the instrument` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "Nothing in this section shall be construed so as to affect"
#ASSERT `s 9(5) section 9 affects the validity or enforceability of the instrument` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- an instrument in the euro-affected currency: see (1) to (3)
#ASSERT `s 9(6)(a) the currency is the euro` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the single currency
#ASSERT `s 9(6)(a) the currency is the euro` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- any other currency: "means"
#ASSERT `s 9(6)(b) the event is the introduction of the euro` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- implementation of economic and monetary union
#ASSERT `s 9(6)(b) the event is the introduction of the euro` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- any other event: "means"
#ASSERT `s 9(6)(c) the body is the EU` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the European Union
#ASSERT `s 9(6)(c) the body is the EU` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- any other body: "means"
#ASSERT `s 9(6)(d) the unit is the Ecu` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the currency basket
#ASSERT `s 9(6)(d) the unit is the Ecu` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- any other unit: "means"
#ASSERT `s 9(6)(e) the reference to the Ecu is replaced by a reference to the euro at a rate of one euro to one Ecu` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- one euro to one Ecu
#ASSERT `s 9(6)(e) the reference to the Ecu is replaced by a reference to the euro at a rate of one euro to one Ecu` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- before the euro first becomes the monetary unit: "when"
#ASSERT `s 9(6)(e) the reference to the Ecu is replaced by a reference to the euro at a rate of one euro to one Ecu` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- an instrument that does not also refer to the definition: see (f)
#ASSERT `s 9(6)(f) the reference to the Ecu is presumed to be a reference to the currency basket` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- no definition: presumed
#ASSERT `s 9(6)(f) the reference to the Ecu is presumed to be a reference to the currency basket` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "unless it is shown that the parties intended otherwise"
#ASSERT `s 9(6)(f) the reference to the Ecu is presumed to be a reference to the currency basket` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- the instrument has the definition: see (e)
